 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of Blau syndrome with a NOD2 variant: \"identified a pathogenic heterozygous NOD2 variant (p. Arg307Trp) which was inherited from his father\".",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; a short Python script only assembled the JSON and the 20 checklist rows per person. Two people: the index boy ('patient', rule 5) and his carrier father ('father of patient', rule 2), who is described only as the source of the variant with 'a history of ankylosing spondylitis'; his disease label is that history, not Blau syndrome. The cDNA c.919C>T is printed only in the Introduction and the protein p. Arg307Trp elsewhere; both are attributed to the patient. For the father only the protein string tied to him is recorded. Patient age at diagnosis taken from '1-year-old' at admission (November 2024) when BS was diagnosed; age at the January 2026 follow-up not stated. 'no ocular or joint abnormalities' / 'No abnormalities were found in the eye and joint examinations' and 'did not exhibit systemic symptoms' are recorded as stated (broad normal examinations, D-27) and not used to exclude the more specific checklist items uveitis, arthritis or fever. n_patients_reported=1 follows the authors' 'a rare case'; the father also carries the variant. No contradictions found.",
